Heeler: rebind the UDP sockets that iOS defuncts while the app is suspended.

iOS defuncts the sockets of an app it suspends. A defunct UDP socket stays
readable, yet every recvfrom fails at once with ENOTCONN and every sendto
with EPIPE. Heeler starts one libzt node per process and never stops it, so
the node outlives every suspension: after the app returns, Phy::poll's
select() reports each of the node's UDP sockets readable, recvfrom fails, the
loop breaks, and select() returns again at once. On an iPhone this pinned a
core (about 41,000 select() calls a second over 16 defunct sockets, each
failing recvfrom with ENOTCONN and sendto with EPIPE) until the process
ended; the node kept working only through sockets bound after the
suspension.

This patch:
- has Phy::poll (Darwin) stop waiting on a UDP socket whose recvfrom fails
  with ENOTCONN or EPIPE (FD_CLR from the read set) and record it, which
  Phy::takeDefunctUdpSocket reports once;
- has NodeService::run, when one was found, close every bound UDP socket
  (Binder::closeAll) and refresh the bindings at once, which binds new
  sockets on the same ports; at most once a second.

Sends to a path whose socket was closed fall back to every bound socket, as
after any binding refresh (Binder::isUdpSocketValid). Each changed file
carries a "Modified by Heeler contributors" notice.

Applies to libzt commit 7e5d0f99a2de81c45faa28e44289bcd19d933bf2 with patch
0002 applied (src/NodeService.cpp) and ZeroTierOne
fc5c3ec22090b5b2a0f274e863651fe9ca489bf4 (1.16.2) in libzt's ext/ZeroTierOne
(osdep/Phy.hpp).

